stage: parser (amplification)
kind: OOM (libFuzzer aborted on malloc(31,675,383,808) ≈ 31 GiB)
site: DexFile::parse — allocation driven by an unchecked header size field
repro: cargo fuzz run fuzz_parser fuzz/crashes/fuzz_parser/oom-c0cb23eb4eaa
size: 3120 bytes

Surfaced during the extended 5-minute smoke. A 3 KiB DEX input drives
parse into a single 31 GiB allocation — classic amplification from a
header count field (string_ids_size, type_ids_size, proto_ids_size,
field_ids_size, method_ids_size, or class_defs_size) not bounded
against the actual file size before being used to pre-allocate a Vec.

Filed for `dex-hardening-sweep`. The general defense: at parse time,
reject any entity count N where N * sizeof(entry) > data.len(). This
same check should cover the two fuzz_cfg / fuzz_ssa OOMs filed
alongside this one, since those amplifications also ride an oversized
count field through parse first.
